# Packaging only. `nytka init` never copies this file into a project.
#
# npm refuses to publish a file named `.gitignore`, AND reads it as pack instructions on the
# way out — so the template's own `private/` rule deleted `private/` from the tarball as the
# `.gitignore` deleted itself. A package scaffolded from the registry arrived with neither,
# while its AGENTS.md still said "`private/` is gitignored", which is a false claim about
# where secrets are safe.
#
# An `.npmignore` overrides `.gitignore` as the ignore source for this directory, and the
# negation puts the file back in the tarball. npm strips `.npmignore` itself, so nothing here
# reaches a consumer. Verified against `npm pack`: 16 of 16 template files ship.
!.gitignore
